        "A fully functional web prototype that acts as an intelligent writing assistant for peer supporters — scoring Emotional Support (ES) and Informational Support (IS) levels in real time and using generative AI to suggest context-aware improvements for safer, more empathetic replies.",
      highlights: [
        { num: "65%", label: "inference latency reduction" },
        { num: "6 yrs", label: "of Reddit data crawled & preprocessed" },
        { num: "3", label: "domain experts for gold-standard annotation" },
        { num: "100k+", label: "posts/comments harvested" },
      ],
      problem:
        "Peer supporters in online mental-health communities write replies that can unintentionally be unsupportive or unsafe. There was no real-time way to measure support quality or ground generative suggestions in evidence, and LLM outputs risked hallucinations and harmful suggestions.",
      roleDetail:
        "Designed the microservice architecture, led dataset construction and expert annotation, fine-tuned the scoring model, built the RAG system, deployed the FastAPI inference service, and implemented the safety-filter middleware and active-learning pipeline.",
      architecture:
        "Microservices: a Flask frontend decoupled from a high-concurrency FastAPI inference service. The inference layer integrates three components — a fine-tuned RoBERTa regression model for ES/IS scoring, a LangChain + ChromaDB + SentenceTransformers RAG system grounding a DeepSeek LLM in retrieved high-quality human responses, and a real-time LLM-based security filtering middleware. Asynchronous request processing runs LLM generation and safety checks in parallel via ThreadPoolExecutor.",
      algorithm:
        "Transfer learning: RoBERTa fine-tuned on an expert-annotated dataset to predict support-quality scores highly correlated with human judgment. Baseline experiments with SVM, Multinomial Logistic Regression, Random Forest, and XGBoost — best IS results with RF, best ES results with XGBoost. RAG retrieval pulls semantically similar high-quality responses to ground the DeepSeek LLM and reduce hallucination.",
      methodology: [
        "Crawled and preprocessed six years of mental-health discussions from Reddit via the Pushshift API.",
        "Led a rigorous annotation effort with three domain experts to label IS/ES metrics, creating a gold-standard training set.",
        "Fine-tuned RoBERTa with transfer learning on the annotated dataset for support-quality scoring.",
        "Built the RAG pipeline with LangChain, ChromaDB, and SentenceTransformers to retrieve and inject evidence into LLM prompts.",
        "Deployed models through a high-concurrency FastAPI service decoupled from the Flask frontend.",
        "Added an automated active-learning loop that filters, pseudo-labels, and folds new submissions back into the training set.",
      ],
      features: [
        "Real-time ES/IS support-quality feedback as users type",
        "Generative AI suggestions grounded in retrieved high-quality responses",
        "Real-time security filter blocking harmful content, self-harm risks, and dangerous medical advice",
        "Automated active-learning pipeline — the model improves without human intervention",
        "Asynchronous parallel inference (LLM + safety checks) for low latency",
      ],
      impact:
        "Optimized inference latency by ~65% via asynchronous processing and parallel execution of LLM generation and security checks. The scoring model correlates strongly with human judgment, and grounding the LLM in retrieved evidence reduced hallucinations and improved suggestion quality.",
      evaluation:
        "IS/ES predictions compared against expert labels across baselines (SVM, MLR, RF, XGBoost) and the fine-tuned RoBERTa; RoBERTa achieved scores highly correlated with human judgment. RAG-grounded outputs were qualitatively evaluated for relevance, safety, and empathy.",
      stack: [
        "Python", "Flask", "FastAPI", "PyTorch", "RoBERTa", "LangChain",
        "DeepSeek LLM", "Sentence Transformers", "ChromaDB", "RAG",
        "Pushshift API", "ThreadPoolExecutor",
      ],
      links: [
        { label: "Live Demo", url: "https://minhazulzju.github.io/BepsBot/", external: true },
      ],
    },
